      "judgment": "Five controls enforce metric-domain admission, strict interval separation, exact singleton equality, independent side positions and correct minimum interval distance. Numeric ordinal domain is not metric. MovingCloser requires after.max<before.min; equal nonsingleton ranges remain indeterminate, not SameDistance. Symmetric equal-distance side crossing can preserve changed position without qualifying distance change. Missing/inactive evidence differs from valid indeterminate assessment; malformed foreign-domain evidence rejects. Read-only distance assessment is not significance, utility, reward or retention authority.",
